At Wed, 17 Jan 2007 19:02:14 -0800,
Tobin Davis wrote:
> 
> What I've seen in the codec reports from testers is the Sigmatel STAC9250 on codec#0,
> the modem on codec#1, and garbage on codec#3 (see attached output).   I've also
> attached some of the dmesg output that was relevant to this issue.

Hm, actually the codecs supported should be up to #2.
So, the patch below should fix the problem.  If it work, I'll push to
ALSA tree.


Takashi

diff -r beb52b12c43f pci/hda/hda_intel.c
--- a/pci/hda/hda_intel.c	Tue Jan 16 17:49:21 2007 +0100
+++ b/pci/hda/hda_intel.c	Thu Jan 18 11:57:43 2007 +0100
@@ -199,7 +199,7 @@ enum { SDI0, SDI1, SDI2, SDI3, SDO0, SDO
 
 /* STATESTS int mask: SD2,SD1,SD0 */
 #define STATESTS_INT_MASK	0x07
-#define AZX_MAX_CODECS		4
+#define AZX_MAX_CODECS		3
 
 /* SD_CTL bits */
 #define SD_CTL_STREAM_RESET	0x01	/* stream reset bit */

